<%# locals: (f:, partner:) %>
<%#
  One action row, at the end of the form, on the page gutter.

  It was rendered twice -- above the accordion and below it -- from raw utility strings rather than
  `essentials_button_classes`. Measured before this: four submit buttons on the page, 36px tall
  rather than the app's 38 because the strings carried no `border`, sitting 0px apart because the
  row had `justify-start` and no `gap`, and inset by `mx-5` while the heading above used the page
  gutter, so the whole form hung 12px to the left of its own title.

  "Save progress" stays. It saves without leaving, which on a thirteen-section form is the
  difference between a form you can put down and one you have to finish in a sitting. It is the
  quiet one, and the primary is last -- design.md.
%>
<div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-slate-200 pt-5">
  <%= f.submit "Save progress",
        class: essentials_button_classes(variant: :secondary, size: :md),
        data: {action: "click->accordion#disableOpenClose"} %>
  <%= f.submit "Save and review", name: "save_review",
        class: essentials_button_classes(variant: :primary, size: :md) %>
</div>
